From: Guohan Lu <securely1g@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Resolve archive tools in the Distroless module context

Generated root APT repositories do not inherit the Distroless module's
zstd_toolchains, bsd_tar_toolchains and gawk apparent repository names.
Resolve those existing declared tools using Label in the owning macro and
use the same gawk label in its location expansion. This preserves archive
commands and targets while avoiding caller mapping failures or shadowing.

Origin: SONiC Database/MACsec analysis failure with rules_distroless
0.9.4.sonic.18. Originally applied after its first 39 ordered patches;
ported after the 41 published patches for the .19 successor. The upstream
archive and all APT source/request/lock bytes are unchanged.
Upstream status: local adaptation, not submitted.

Signed-off-by: Guohan Lu <securely1g@gmail.com>

--- a/apt/private/deb_postfix.bzl
+++ b/apt/private/deb_postfix.bzl
@@ -21,7 +21,8 @@
         ;;
     esac
 """
-    toolchains = ["@zstd_toolchains//:resolved_toolchain"]
+    # Resolve tools in this module, not in generated APT caller repositories.
+    toolchains = [Label("@zstd_toolchains//:resolved_toolchain")]
     tools = []
 
     # If mergedusr, then rewrite paths to hoist bins/libs from / of the fs to /usr counterpart.
@@ -34,8 +35,9 @@
     # Mapping taken from https://github.com/floppym/merge-usr/blob/15dd02207bdee7ca6720d7024e8c0ffdc166ed23/merge-usr#L17-L25
     # https://salsa.debian.org/md/usrmerge/-/tree/master/debian?ref_type=heads
     if mergedusr:
-        toolchains = ["@bsd_tar_toolchains//:resolved_toolchain"]
-        tools.append("@gawk//:resolved_toolchain")
+        toolchains = [Label("@bsd_tar_toolchains//:resolved_toolchain")]
+        gawk = Label("@gawk//:resolved_toolchain")
+        tools.append(gawk)
         apply = """\
             $(BSDTAR_BIN) --confirmation --gzip --options 'gzip:!timestamp' -cf "$$layer" \
             -s "#^\\./bin/\\(.\\)#./usr/bin/\\1#" \
@@ -45,7 +47,7 @@
             -s "#^\\./lib64/\\(.\\)#./usr/lib64/\\1#" \
             -s "#^\\./libx32/\\(.\\)#./usr/libx32/\\1#" \
             "@$$data_file" 2< <(
-                $(BSDTAR_BIN) -tvf "$$data_file" | $(location @gawk//:resolved_toolchain) '{
+                $(BSDTAR_BIN) -tvf "$$data_file" | $(location %s) '{
                     ORS=""
                     keep="y"
                     if (substr($$1, 1, 1) == "d" && (\\
@@ -62,7 +64,7 @@
                     fflush()
                 }'
             )
-        """
+        """ % gawk
 
     native.genrule(
         name = name,
